[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Center Game"]
[Variation "Center Game: Paulsen Attack Variation"]
[ECO "C22"]
[Character "solid"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "tempo-on-queen,development"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. e4 e5 2. d4 exd4
3. Qxd4 { White recaptures with the queen. It will be chased away, which costs White time. }
3... Nc6 { Develops with an attack on the queen. }
4. Qe3 ( 4. Qa4 Nf6 ) ( 4. Qd3 Nf6 )
4... Nf6 { Develops with an attack on e4. The queen must now guard that pawn, and on e3 it blocks its own bishop. }
5. Nc3 5... Bb4 { Pins the knight to the king. There is no pawn on d2, so the bishop on b4 looks straight at the king. }
6. Bd2 6... O-O { Gets the king out of the middle. }
7. O-O-O 7... Re8 { Puts the rook on the e-file, where it pressures e4 and the queen. }
8. Bc4 8... d6 { Opens the c8 bishop and covers e5. Plan: ...Bg4 or ...Be6 to trade White's bishop, with the rook on e8 ready to punish any careless move that leaves e4 loose. } *
